From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:30:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 391/400] TechDraw: deleting a page removes its views, sections
 and dimensions

The view's removal of its hatches and dimensions used {} in a printf
format (Unknown document '{}'); the page's loop now removes its views by
name, each looked up again; a group's anchor removed with the group is
not a corrupt group.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Mod/TechDraw/App/DrawPage.cpp      | 18 ++++++++-----
 src/Mod/TechDraw/App/DrawProjGroup.cpp |  1 +
 src/Mod/TechDraw/App/DrawViewPart.cpp  |  8 +++---
 src/Mod/Unified/TestDrawingPdf.py      | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Mod/TechDraw/App/DrawPage.cpp b/src/Mod/TechDraw/App/DrawPage.cpp
index 5082d566e..4c75e6ceb 100644
--- a/src/Mod/TechDraw/App/DrawPage.cpp
+++ b/src/Mod/TechDraw/App/DrawPage.cpp
@@ -432,12 +432,18 @@ void DrawPage::unsetupObject()
     std::string pageName = getNameInDocument();
 
     try {
-        for (auto& v : Views.getValues()) {
-            //NOTE: the order of objects in Page.Views does not reflect the object hierarchy
-            //      this means that a ProjGroup could be deleted before its child ProjGroupItems.
-            //      this causes problems when removing objects from document
-            if (v->isAttachedToDocument()) {
-                std::string viewName = v->getNameInDocument();
+        //NOTE: the order of objects in Page.Views does not reflect the object hierarchy
+        //      this means that a ProjGroup could be deleted before its child ProjGroupItems.
+        //      a view removes others with it (a group its items, a view its dimensions):
+        //      by name, each looked up again before it is removed
+        std::vector<std::string> viewNames;
+        for (auto* v : Views.getValues()) {
+            if (v && v->isAttachedToDocument()) {
+                viewNames.emplace_back(v->getNameInDocument());
+            }
+        }
+        for (const auto& viewName : viewNames) {
+            if (doc->getObject(viewName.c_str())) {
                 Base::Interpreter().runStringArg("App.getDocument(\"%s\").removeObject(\"%s\")",
                                                  docName.c_str(), viewName.c_str());
             }
